&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49609593</guid><pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:45:22 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: AI means the end of software as we know it</title><link>https://github.com/jamison/ilc/blob/main/HUMANS.md</link><description>&lt;p&gt;As agents scale in intelligence per token per watt, software architecture is starting to shift: away from CRUD databases and directional tree structures, toward multidimensional hypergraphs where knowledge, governance, and code are all the same kind of node. No single human can hold that structure in their head at once — but an agent can traverse it at inference speed. ILC is our open-source infrastructure project: a self-compiling morphogenetic hypergraph where the software literally builds itself from the same structure it uses to organize knowledge and settle it's own governance and disputes. Thinking and code, becoming one thing.. This ILC open source project is moving the needle towards that. Thanks for your critical feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
